NAME='Mercury'
COVER_SUB='How your mind works in each sign.'
T=[
('Quick-witted','Mercury in Aries brings initiative, intellectual curiosity and a taste for any profession that tests the mind. Thought is quick and so is speech: a critical edge, witty polemic and no fear of a challenge. Jyotish rates Mars neutral toward Mercury. Under strain, it turns to bluff and sterile contradiction, and to enemies made by a sharp tongue. Karmic reading: a mind that learned to defend itself and now learns to listen. Science and mathematics, long linked to Mercury, favour fast, pioneering ideas. The lesson: a good idea survives a pause.'),
('Slow and sure','Mercury in Taurus develops a strong practical sense: studies are chosen with a view to a profitable activity, and the mind has a good memory, a feeling for art and a sense of opportunity, handled with tact and diplomacy. Jyotish counts Venus as Mercury’s friend, so the sign is comfortable. Thought moves slowly, and once made up it is hard to change. Under strain, it lacks practicality. Karmic reading: a mind that learned to value what is concrete. The shadow is stubbornness. The lesson: changing your mind is a sign of strength.'),
('Own sign','Mercury is at home in Gemini, its own daytime house, and Jyotish agrees. It gives great ease in learning, oratory and an extraordinary power to convince. Assimilation is fast, the intelligence remarkable and the person can emerge in almost any field of knowledge, noticed for merit more than for ambition, with an engaging charm. Karmic reading: a mind that has been a messenger in many lives. The shadow is scattering, gossip and knowing a little about everything. The lesson: depth is also a kind of cleverness.'),
('Feeling mind','Mercury in Cancer, in the Moon’s house, works passively and gives room to a fervent creativity. Diplomacy is spontaneous, sometimes simulated, aimed at reaching goals, and memory for family stories is excellent. Jyotish counts the Moon as Mercury’s enemy, so head and heart can quarrel. Under strain, it leans to melancholy, discouragement and utopian ideas. Karmic reading: a mind shaped by childhood and inherited stories. The shadow is taking things personally and talking in circles around a worry. The lesson: say the feeling out loud, plainly.'),
('Dramatic','Mercury in Leo, in the Sun’s house, brings great openness of mind and no pettiness. An exceptional gift for relationships predisposes to success, especially in careers that put you in the spotlight. Many interests are pursued with constancy, with good nervous balance, determination and a facility for foreign languages. Jyotish counts the Sun as Mercury’s friend. Karmic reading: a mind learning to speak from the heart. The shadow is talking over others and hating to be corrected. The lesson: listening is also a form of leadership.'),
('Own sign and exalted','Mercury is both at home and exalted in Virgo, and Jyotish gives it exaltation, own-sign and moolatrikona strength here at once: its strongest place. The mind is trained for analysis and synthesis, with logic, clarity, eloquence and tact, favouring a career in business or politics, and an aptitude for philosophy, esotericism and exact science. Karmic reading: a mind that has refined its craft over many lives. The shadow is worry, nitpicking and paralysis by analysis. The lesson: a useful answer is better than a perfect one.'),
('Fair-minded','Mercury in Libra gives good moral balance, a deep sense of justice and high intelligence, with a gift for legal and political study, especially with Jupiter, and a taste for art with Venus. Jyotish counts Venus as Mercury’s friend. You weigh both sides before you speak and are tactful, a natural mediator. Under strain, judgement suffers. Karmic reading: a mind learning to decide. The shadow is indecision and telling people what they want to hear. The lesson: fairness sometimes means taking a side.'),
('Probing','Mercury in Scorpio, when well aspected, shows intelligence above average, a strongly intuitive mind and certain success in whatever career is chosen, with talent for investigation, politics, medicine and above all psychology, and an interest in esoteric science. Jyotish rates Mars neutral. Words dig under the surface and rarely say everything. Under strain: greed and suspicion. Karmic reading: a mind exploring secrets and the shadow. The lesson: share what you have found, not only what you have noticed.'),
('Detriment','Mercury in Sagittarius is in detriment: tradition sees it in exile, yet neutral or well aspected it favours intelligence, an interest in religion and philosophy, and brings success in trade, foreign contacts, travel and languages. Jyotish counts Jupiter as neutral to Mercury. The mind sees the big picture but can miss the details. Under strain: overestimating your abilities. Karmic reading: a mind learning to turn belief into knowledge. The shadow is preaching and skipping the fine print. The lesson: check the facts before you announce the truth.'),
('Practical','Mercury in slow, methodical Capricorn loses agility and expansiveness, yet the intelligence stays alive and the spirit is guarded. Study and work are favoured: a reflective, patient mind suited to meticulous research, mathematics, philosophy and exact science. Jyotish rates Saturn neutral toward Mercury. You think in plans, structure and consequences, and your humour is dry. Karmic reading: a mind disciplined by earlier hardship. The shadow is pessimism and a cold tone. The lesson: encouragement is also useful information.'),
('Inventive','Mercury in Aquarius, when harmonious, shows excellent nervous and mental balance, with brilliant and deep ideas that lead to independent professions needing imagination, practical sense and individualism. You find the best solution to any predicament. Jyotish rates Saturn neutral toward Mercury. Under strain: nervousness that can turn to spite, and impatient ambition. Karmic reading: a mind designed for the future. The shadow is intellectual detachment. The lesson: a new idea also needs a human audience.'),
('Detriment and fall','Mercury is in both detriment and fall in Pisces, and Jyotish marks its debilitation here, deepest at 15°. The mind works by intuition, sensitivity and imagery more than logic, with artistic gifts, an attraction to the paranormal, mediumistic abilities and a gift for professions that care for others. Facts can slip away and plans become fog. Karmic reading: a mind remembering what words cannot carry. The shadow is vagueness and avoiding hard conversations. The lesson: write it down and say it clearly.'),
]
